{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when you err.</b> It has already been explained in the received tradition that Scripture speaks of an error involving idolatry. This is because, since it was decreed upon them that He would scatter their seed among the nations (Psalms 106:27), it was unavoidable that they would err in idolatry upon their return to their land." "<b>And you do not perform all these commandments that YHWH spoke to Moses.</b> Since you err in idolatry — even if you perform all the actions of the commandments, you do not perform those commandments that YHWH spoke to Moses. For He, blessed be He, preceded them all with knowledge of His divinity, saying אָנֹכִי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ (Exodus 20:2). And so the Sages of blessed memory said: 'One who acknowledges idolatry is as one who denies the entire Torah in its entirety' (Sifrei 111)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:00.147539379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}